       "content": "```python\ndef correct_bracketing(brackets: str):\n    \"\"\" brackets is a string of \"(\" and \")\".\n    return True if every opening bracket has a corresponding closing bracket.\n\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"(\")\n    False\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"()\")\n    True\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"(()())\")\n    True\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\")(()\")\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for ch in brackets:\n        if ch == \"(\":\n            count += 1\n        elif ch == \")\":\n            count -= 1\n        if count < 0:\n            return False\n    return count == 0\n```",
       "name": null,
       "reasoning": "The task is to implement a function that checks if a string of brackets is correctly bracketed. I need to verify that every opening bracket has a corresponding closing bracket in the correct order.\n\nThe approach:\n1. Use a counter (or stack) to track the balance of brackets.\n2. Iterate through each character:\n   - If it's \"(\", increment the counter\n   - If it's \")\", decrement the counter\n   - If the counter ever goes negative, it means we have a closing bracket without a matching opening one, so return False\n3. At the end, return True if the counter is 0 (all brackets matched), False otherwise.\n\nLet me verify with the examples:\n- \"(\" \u2192 counter goes to 1, ends at 1 \u2192 False \u2713\n- \"()\" \u2192 counter goes 1, 0 \u2192 True \u2713\n- \"(()())\" \u2192 counter: 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 0 \u2192 True \u2713\n- \")(()\" \u2192 counter: -1 \u2192 immediately False \u2713\n\nThis is straightforward.",
       "reasoning_content": "The task is to implement a function that checks if a string of brackets is correctly bracketed. I need to verify that every opening bracket has a corresponding closing bracket in the correct order.\n\nThe approach:\n1. Use a counter (or stack) to track the balance of brackets.\n2. Iterate through each character:\n   - If it's \"(\", increment the counter\n   - If it's \")\", decrement the counter\n   - If the counter ever goes negative, it means we have a closing bracket without a matching opening one, so return False\n3. At the end, return True if the counter is 0 (all brackets matched), False otherwise.\n\nLet me verify with the examples:\n- \"(\" \u2192 counter goes to 1, ends at 1 \u2192 False \u2713\n- \"()\" \u2192 counter goes 1, 0 \u2192 True \u2713\n- \"(()())\" \u2192 counter: 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 0 \u2192 True \u2713\n- \")(()\" \u2192 counter: -1 \u2192 immediately False \u2713\n\nThis is straightforward.",
